ConPTY takes signed 16-bit dimensions, while PtySize holds u16. Refuse dimensions above i16::MAX before
creating or resizing a pseudoconsole, with the original requested size in the error instead of wrapped numbers.
The zero-size API errors and the last successful size are left as they were.

ngterm's own. Remove when portable-pty checks the COORD range before converting a PtySize. Tests:
ngterm-pty's an_oversized_console_is_refused_with_the_requested_size and a_resize_the_console_refuses_is_reported.

